---
import BaseCard from '@components/base/base-card.astro';
import Container from '@components/base/container.astro';
---

<section class='py-8 sm:py-12'>
  <Container class='flex flex-col gap-6'>
    <!-- Page header -->
    <div class='px-1'>
      <h1 class='text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground'>
        me<span class='text-muted-foreground'>.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class='mt-1 text-sm text-subtle'>
        a developer, occasionally a human being.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary -->
    <BaseCard title='[ summary ]'>
      <div class='flex flex-col gap-5'>
        <div
          class='flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground'
        >
          <p>
            Hey — I'm Luu. A software developer who spends most of his time
            building things that are fast, minimal, and (hopefully) actually
            useful. I like clean APIs, boring infrastructure that just works,
            and UIs that don't scream for attention.
          </p>
          <p>
            When I'm not staring at a terminal, I'm probably reading about
            something I'll never implement, convincing myself that <em>this</em>
            side project will be different, or falling down a rabbit hole on how some
            system underneath the surface actually works.
          </p>
          <p>
            I care a lot about the craft — readable code, good defaults, and not
            making the next person who reads my code want to quit.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Quote -->
        <blockquote
          class='border-l-2 border-edge pl-4 text-sm italic text-subtle'
        >
          <p>
            "Programs must be written for people to read, and only incidentally
            for machines to execute."
          </p>
          <footer class='mt-2 not-italic text-muted'>
            — Harold Abelson, <cite
              >Structure and Interpretation of Computer Programs</cite
            >
          </footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </BaseCard>

    <!-- What I'm up to now -->
    <BaseCard title='[ now ]'>
      <ul class='flex flex-col gap-3'>
        <li class='flex items-center gap-3 text-sm'>
          <span class='shrink-0 font-mono text-foreground'>[o]</span>
          <span class='text-muted-foreground'>
            Working as a <span class='text-foreground'>Software Engineer</span> —
            building backend services, wrangling APIs, and the occasional infrastructure
            rabbit hole.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class='flex items-center gap-3 text-sm'>
          <span class='shrink-0 font-mono text-foreground'>[*]</span>
          <span class='text-muted-foreground'>
            Trying to get better at
            <span class='text-foreground'>system design</span> — reading more, thinking
            more, building more.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class='flex items-center gap-3 text-sm'>
          <span class='shrink-0 font-mono text-foreground'>[*]</span>
          <span class='text-muted-foreground'>
            Building this site as an excuse to dig into
            <span class='text-foreground'>Astro + SolidJS</span> and make something
            I'm actually proud of.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class='flex items-center gap-3 text-sm'>
          <span class='shrink-0 font-mono text-foreground'>[*]</span>
          <span class='text-muted-foreground'>
            Slowly learning <span class='text-foreground'>Rust</span> without crying
            too much. Progress is being made.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class='flex items-center gap-3 text-sm'>
          <span class='shrink-0 font-mono text-subtle'>[-]</span>
          <span class='text-subtle'>
            still figuring out what I actually want to do long term. that's
            fine.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </BaseCard>

    <!-- Experiences -->
    <BaseCard title='[ experiences ]'>
      <div class='flex flex-col divide-y divide-edge'>
        <!-- Current job -->
        <div class='flex flex-col gap-3 pb-6'>
          <div
            class='flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between'
          >
            <div class='flex items-center gap-2'>
              <span class='font-mono text-xs text-subtle'>[o]</span>
              <span class='text-sm font-medium text-foreground'>
                Software Engineer
              </span>
              <span class='text-subtle text-sm'>@</span>
              <span class='text-sm text-foreground'>COMPANY_NAME</span>
            </div>
            <span class='ml-5 font-mono text-xs text-subtle sm:ml-0'>
              2024 — present
            </span>
          </div>
          <ul class='ml-5 flex flex-col gap-1.5'>
            <li class='flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground'>
              <span class='mt-1.5 h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subtle'
              ></span>
              <span>
                Build and maintain backend services handling core business logic
                and internal APIs used across multiple teams.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class='flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground'>
              <span class='mt-1.5 h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subtle'
              ></span>
              <span>
                Worked on improving system reliability — better observability,
                cleaner error handling, reducing the "why is this broken"
                moments.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class='flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground'>
              <span class='mt-1.5 h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subtle'
              ></span>
              <span>
                Collaborated on frontend integration work, bridging the gap
                between backend contracts and UI requirements.
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class='ml-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2'>
            {
              [
                'TypeScript',
                'Node.js',
                'PostgreSQL',
                'Docker',
                'REST APIs',
              ].map((tag) => (
                <span class='font-mono text-xs text-subtle border border-edge px-2 py-0.5 rounded-sm'>
                  {tag}
                </span>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Internship -->
        <div class='flex flex-col gap-3 pt-6'>
          <div
            class='flex flex-col gap-1 sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between'
          >
            <div class='flex items-center gap-2'>
              <span class='font-mono text-xs text-subtle'>[*]</span>
              <span class='text-sm font-medium text-foreground'>
                Software Engineer Intern
              </span>
              <span class='text-subtle text-sm'>@</span>
              <span class='text-sm text-foreground'>COMPANY_NAME</span>
            </div>
            <span class='ml-5 font-mono text-xs text-subtle sm:ml-0'>
              2023 — 2024
            </span>
          </div>
          <ul class='ml-5 flex flex-col gap-1.5'>
            <li class='flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground'>
              <span class='mt-1.5 h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subtle'
              ></span>
              <span>
                First real exposure to production code — learned quickly that
                reading existing code is harder than writing new code.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class='flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground'>
              <span class='mt-1.5 h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subtle'
              ></span>
              <span>
                Contributed to frontend features, fixed bugs that had been
                silently lurking, and wrote tests for things nobody had tested.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class='flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground'>
              <span class='mt-1.5 h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-subtle'
              ></span>
              <span>
                Got comfortable with code review cycles, git workflows, and the
                art of writing PR descriptions that people actually read.
              </span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class='ml-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2'>
            {
              ['React', 'JavaScript', 'REST APIs', 'Git'].map((tag) => (
                <span class='font-mono text-xs text-subtle border border-edge px-2 py-0.5 rounded-sm'>
                  {tag}
                </span>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </BaseCard>
  </Container>
</section>
